      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Well, I suppose what brought me in is that I just keep getting up in meetings or at dinner when everyone else is seated. Like, I'll suddenly feel the need to refill my coffee or go check a handout. I teach secondary school, you know, and we just got these new curriculum handouts from the district. Honestly, they are so poorly formatted. The font is incredibly tiny, and they used this glossy paper that just glares under the fluorescent lights in my classroom. I brought it up to the principal, but you know how administration is, they just nod and do absolutely nothing about it. \n\nBut anyway, what was I saying? Oh, right, getting up. Yes, I'll just suddenly stand up and walk to the back of the room during a staff meeting, or pop up from the dinner table, even though nothing is actually urgent. My husband finally suggested I should probably come talk to someone about it.",
