      "patient_response": "Careless mistakes? No, I wouldn't say that. I'm actually quite meticulous, especially with my grading. You really have to be, otherwise the students will argue with you over every single half-point. I always use a purple pen for grading now—they told us at a professional development seminar a few years ago that red ink is too aggressive and damages the students' self-esteem. Can you imagine? Red ink being aggressive. \n\nAnyway, I used to get these absolutely wonderful Japanese gel pens from a little stationery shop downtown. It was such a lovely store, smelled just like fresh paper and binding glue. But they closed down during the pandemic, which was just a tragedy. It’s an artisanal bakery now. They do make a very nice sourdough, I have to admit. My husband picked up a loaf just this past Saturday and we made the most incredible grilled cheese sandwiches with this sharp cheddar we found at the farmer's market... \n\nOh, dear, I'm doing it again, aren't I? What was the question? Focus! Right. No, my focus is perfectly fine, and I don't really make careless errors. I just can't seem to stay in my chair.",
